The failure report must include:
1. Test Identification — test name, date, component, test facility
2. Test Objective — what was being verified
3. Failure Description — what went wrong, observed vs expected behavior
4. Failure Analysis — likely root cause, contributing factors
5. Impact Assessment — effect on component acceptance, schedule, and downstream integration
6. Data Summary — key metrics showing the failure in tabular form
7. Corrective Actions — recommended rework or retest steps
8. NPR Implications — which NPR requirements are not satisfied due to this failure
9. Disposition Recommendation — rework, retest, replace, or use-as-is with rationale

Write a complete, realistic failure report. Be specific about the failure mode.
